Below is a **complete, production‑ready skeleton** for a **modular Cloud‑Native API‑Gateway** written in **C# / .NET 8**.  
The solution is split into three logical modules (projects) that can be versioned, unit‑tested, and deployed independently:

| Module | Responsibility | Main NuGet Packages |
|--------|----------------|---------------------|
| **Gateway.Api** | ASP.NET Core host that wires everything together | `Microsoft.AspNetCore.App`, `Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting` |
| **Gateway.ReverseProxy** | YARP‑based reverse‑proxy that forwards to downstream clusters | `Microsoft.ReverseProxy` |
| **Gateway.Security** | JWT validation + scope‑based authorization | `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer`, `System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt` |
| **Gateway.Tracing** | OpenTelemetry distributed‑tracing + correlation‑ID injection | `OpenTelemetry.Extensions.Hosting`, `OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.AspNetCore`, `OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Http` |

> **Why this layout?**  
> *Each module has a single responsibility, can be unit‑tested in isolation and swapped out (e.g., replace YARP with Envoy).  
> *All modules expose **extension methods** (`AddGateway…`) that the host (`Gateway.Api`) calls – this is the “plug‑and‑play” pattern that makes the gateway truly modular.*

---

## 1️⃣ Folder / Project Structure

```
/GatewaySolution
│
├─ src
│   ├─ Gateway.Api/                (ASP.NET Core host)
│   ├─ Gateway.ReverseProxy/       (YARP reverse‑proxy)
│   ├─ Gateway.Security/           (JWT authz)
│   └─ Gateway.Tracing/            (OpenTelemetry + Correlation)
│
├─ tests
│   ├─ Gateway.Security.Tests/
│   └─ Gateway.ReverseProxy.Tests/
│
└─ docker-compose.yml
```

> **Tip:** Use `dotnet new sln` → `dotnet new web` / `dotnet new classlib` to create the projects, then add them to the solution.

---

